---
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CatalogCard from '../../../components/CatalogCard.astro';
import CategoryHubDetail from '../../../components/product/CategoryHubDetail.astro';
import StatusNotice from '../../../components/StatusNotice.astro';
import { getGroup, productHref, productsInGroup } from '../../../data/products.js';
import { productImageAlt } from '../../../utils/product-page.js';
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const group = getGroup('iso-resins');
const items = productsInGroup('iso-resins');
---
<Base
  title="ISO Resins — Isophthalic Resin Supplier in Nepal"
  description="Isophthalic resin products supplied and imported by Samrat FRP Traders for buyers across Nepal. ISO here means isophthalic acid, not an ISO certification."
>
  <section class="page-hero hero-shell">
    <div class="hero-grid-lines" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container page-hero-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product category</p>
      <h1>{group.name}</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">{group.summary}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { label: 'Home', href: '/en/' },
          { label: 'Products', href: '/en/products/' },
          { label: group.name },
        ]}
      />

      <div class="category-intro" data-reveal>
        <p>
          The letters cause more confusion than anything else in the catalogue, so they are worth settling first.
          ISO here is isophthalic acid, one of the raw materials used to build the polyester backbone. It is a
          chemistry description, not a certification, and it is unrelated to ISO 9001. A supplier may hold that
          certificate separately, but it certifies a quality management system rather than the performance of a
          resin batch.
        </p>
        <p>
          What the isophthalic backbone buys is resistance to hydrolysis, the slow attack water makes on ester
          linkages over years of contact. That is why the industry specifies an isophthalic grade for laminates
          that stay wet or hold chemicals, and why paying for one on a dry indoor panel rarely earns its cost.
          Everything else about working with it is familiar: it is still an unsaturated polyester, still cured at
          workshop temperature with a peroxide catalyst.
        </p>
        <p>
          This category holds the isophthalic laminating resin. Two other products in the range are isophthalic in
          chemistry but belong to their families by what they do rather than by their names: ISO Gelcoat is a
          surface layer and sits under <a href="/en/products/gelcoat/">Gelcoat</a>, and ISO Fire Retardant Resin is
          chosen for fire performance and sits under <a href="/en/products/fire-retardant-resins/">Fire Retardant
          Resins</a>. Supplier documentation for the grade below is not yet in our library, so no figures for it
          are published anywhere on this site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <StatusNotice
        title="Supplier documentation"
        message="Technical data sheets and safety data sheets are linked from each product page. Supplier technical data is attributed to the issuer and is not a Samrat FRP Traders certification."
      />

      <div class="category-grid" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        {items.map((product) => (
          <CatalogCard
            name={product.name}
            eyebrow={group.name}
            href={productHref(product, '/en')}
            showMedia
            image={product.images?.[0]}
            imageAlt={productImageAlt(product, false)}
            ctaLabel="View product"
          />
        ))}
      </div>

      <CategoryHubDetail groupSlug="iso-resins" lang="en" />

      <div class="section-actions" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <a class="button" href="/en/resources/what-is-isophthalic-polyester-resin/">What is isophthalic resin?</a>
        <a class="button" href="/en/products/">View full catalogue</a>
        <a class="button" href="/en/contact/">Send an enquiry</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Product-discovery priority: get real product photography in view
     quickly rather than running the full-height brand hero every other
     page uses. Scoped to this page only. */
  .page-hero {
    min-height: clamp(14rem, 26vh, 19rem);
  }

  .page-hero-content {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .section:first-of-type {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .category-intro {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-block: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .category-intro p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .category-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(16rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
</style>
